            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "> I've been shopping around for a plugin that will let me zoom into a buffer, like mini.misc.zoom() does! Of course I should have expected that mini would have what I was looking for :D\r\n\r\nhere [`Misc.zoom()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f1dd64cf2ac1b348bd440e59446abf680c7188d6/doc/mini-misc.txt#L268-L279) I'm not sure if you're looking for sample code, but you can search for that [`x`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aclosed%20label%3Amini.misc%20zoom).\r\n\r\n>I also use dropbar.nvim, and I'm wondering if there is any way to zoom into the buffer but maintain my custom winbar? It really helps me to have it there to remember what file I'm working in. I will add that it reappears if I hit space.\r\n\r\nIf you already have a plan for that [`X`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/983), or you can also use it like this: `vim.opt.winbar=“%{%v:lua.vim.fn.expand(”%“)%}”`",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've been shopping around for a plugin that will let me zoom into a buffer, like mini.misc.zoom() does! Of course I should have expected that mini would have what I was looking for :D</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">here <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f1dd64cf2ac1b348bd440e59446abf680c7188d6/doc/mini-misc.txt#L268-L279\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Misc.zoom()</code></a> I'm not sure if you're looking for sample code, but you can search for that <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aclosed%20label%3Amini.misc%20zoom\"><code class=\"notranslate\">x</code></a>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also use dropbar.nvim, and I'm wondering if there is any way to zoom into the buffer but maintain my custom winbar? It really helps me to have it there to remember what file I'm working in. I will add that it reappears if I hit space.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you already have a plan for that <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/983\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/983/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">X</code></a>, or you can also use it like this: <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.opt.winbar=“%{%v:lua.vim.fn.expand(”%“)%}”</code></p>",
            "bodyText": "I've been shopping around for a plugin that will let me zoom into a buffer, like mini.misc.zoom() does! Of course I should have expected that mini would have what I was looking for :D\n\nhere Misc.zoom() I'm not sure if you're looking for sample code, but you can search for that x.\n\nI also use dropbar.nvim, and I'm wondering if there is any way to zoom into the buffer but maintain my custom winbar? It really helps me to have it there to remember what file I'm working in. I will add that it reappears if I hit space.\n\nIf you already have a plan for that X, or you can also use it like this: vim.opt.winbar=“%{%v:lua.vim.fn.expand(”%“)%}”",
